{"authored" [{"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :q